# ralph-config.md

Ralph reads the block below for deploy URL, git remote, and validation commands.

```ralph-config
RALPH_GIT_REMOTE="[your HTTPS git remote]"
RALPH_GIT_MAIN_BRANCH="main"
RALPH_DEPLOY_URL="[your dev/staging URL]"
RALPH_DEPLOY_WAIT_SECONDS=300
RALPH_VALIDATE_LOCAL="npm run check"
RALPH_VALIDATE_DEPLOY="npm test"
RALPH_HEALTH_CHECK_PATH="/health"
RALPH_TEST_ENV_VARS="STAGING_URL=$RALPH_DEPLOY_URL"
```

## Stack Standards

Ralph follows these patterns on every task. Edit for your stack.

**Routes:** auth → validate → execute → respond. 400 validation, 500 server, 401 auth. Never expose stack traces.
**Secrets:** .env is local and gitignored. .env.example is committed. Fail fast if missing — no silent fallbacks.
**Schema:** Validate at request/response boundaries only. Optional fields safe to add; required fields need migration/default.
**Selectors:** data-testid > role > label > text. Never generated IDs (e.g. :rg: breaks CSS selectors).
**Async:** waitForFunction for computed values — button visible ≠ data loaded.
**Tests:** Update inline with implementation changes. Visual validation required for UI tasks (wait for deploy, open browser).
**Docs:** README.md for dirs with multiple files. Doc comments on changed public APIs.
